# Repo Codex Brief — FFPy

> Generated by ai-enrich on 2026-05-06.

## Current Priorities

- Pick'em web app (`ffpy-pickem-web`): FastAPI + Vue strategy tester with
  optional Supabase auth. See `docs/security/SUPABASE_HARDENED_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`.
- Lineup optimizer comparison: PuLP/CBC vs FICO Xpress (notebooks under
  `notebooks/`, e.g. `xpress_vs_pulp_ff_lineup.ipynb`).
- Historical projections: improve `HistoricalProjectionModel` (currently
  weighted average + ±5% variance over last N weeks).

## Start Here

- `AI-CONTEXT.md` (repo root) — token-condensed module-by-module map.
- `CLAUDE.md` — primary onboarding doc and durable repo rules.
- `README.md` — quickstart, make targets, env vars.
- `.claude/wiki/index.md` — wiki catalog (when populated).

## Default Working Mode

- Prefer implementation over speculation.
- Decompose substantial work into atomic tasks with clear file ownership.
- Call out blockers, risks, and assumptions explicitly.
- Run `make check` (ruff + pytest) before declaring work done.

## Architecture Preferences

- SQLite at `~/.ffpy/ffpy.db` is the source of truth for stats; nflverse
  pulls are reproducible via `make db.load SEASON=YYYY`.
- Schema migrations under `src/ffpy/migrations/` are append-only — never
  edit a merged migration.
- New analytical features should land in `src/ffpy/` as importable
  modules first, then exposed via Streamlit pages or the pickem web app —
  not as one-off notebook scripts.
- Notebooks under `notebooks/` are for exploration; promote stable code
  into `src/ffpy/`.

## Output Preferences

- Concise summaries first.
- Include exact file paths and `path:line` references.
- Show verification status (tests run, lint clean) and any gaps.

## Verification Bias

- Run `make lint` and `make test` (or the narrower `uv run pytest tests/test_X.py`)
  for the touched area.
- For UI / Streamlit changes, type-checking and tests verify code
  correctness, not feature correctness — say so when the UI was not
  exercised manually.

## High-Value Paths

- `src/ffpy/` — application code (app, optimizer, projections, scoring,
  database, integrations, pickem, nflverse_loader)
- `src/ffpy/migrations/` — SQL schema (versioned)
- `src/ffpy/pages/` — Streamlit multipage UI
- `tests/` — pytest suite (`test_scoring.py`, `test_optimizer.py`)
- `config/` — JSON presets for scoring + roster
- `examples/` — runnable demos
- `notebooks/` — exploration only; promote to `src/ffpy/` when stable
- `.claude/wiki/pages/` — durable knowledge graph
